{
  "name": "incinerator",
  "description": "An implementation of the Ueno-Ohori concurrent, exact, and non-moving garbage collector in Rust, based on the ICFP'16 research paper. It utilizes tree-structured bitmaps for mark-bit management and a sophisticated handshake mechanism to synchronize mutator threads with the collector. The library provides a segmented heap architecture with size-class partitioning and write barriers to ensure memory safety in highly concurrent environments.",
